            <div xml:id="d1489">

                <pb facs="1122" n="1006" xml:id="pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.12/24.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Brazilian Minister to Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Your 79, July 8. Department has been pleased to instruct American Consul
                    General, Monterey, again urgently to bring to attention of Constitutionalist
                    Chief advisability of extending full protection to persons connected with
                    religious organizations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
